Online payments in Colombia are split between bank transfers, wallets and cards. Worldpay’s Global Payments Report 2025 puts account-to-account payments, led by PSE online bank transfers, at 28% of e-commerce value in 2024, digital wallets at 26%, credit cards at 22%, debit and prepaid cards at 14% and cash (cash on delivery and pay-in-cash vouchers) at 8%. Wallets have grown quickly: Nequi was used by 54% of online shoppers surveyed, PayPal by 25% and DaviPlata by 22%. Bre-B, the Banco de la República’s interoperable instant payment system, entered full operation on 6 October 2025, adding instant transfers to keys (llaves) such as a phone number and interoperable QR codes. Prices are in Colombian pesos (COP). To convert, merchants typically need PSE, local credit and debit cards, Nequi and DaviPlata, and a cash option.
