- All five criteria (A–E) must be met: Criterion A requires deficits in all three social-communication components; Criterion B requires at least two of four restricted/repetitive features (sensory hyper-/hypo-reactivity was newly added in DSM-5).
- The DSM-5-TR uses three severity levels — 1 'requiring support,' 2 'requiring substantial support,' 3 'requiring very substantial support' — mapped to support needs, not to the old labels (the Asperger's-to-Level-1 mapping is rough and should not be taught as exact).
- Code Criterion A and Criterion B severity separately — collapsing them into one overall number is the most common documentation error, because the mismatch (e.g., low social-support need with high sensory/rigidity need) is the most useful information (APA, 2022, DSM-5-TR).
- Document the required specifiers: with/without intellectual impairment, with/without language impairment, associated genetic/medical condition or environmental factor (e.g., valproate), associated neurodevelopmental/mental disorder, and catatonia.
