# Sensory Symptoms of Autism Spectrum Disorder
...
2019 

Abnormal sensory symptoms, such as sensitivity to sound, smell, taste, and touch, occur with a range of neurodevelopmental conditions including autism spectrum disorder (ASD), attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD), and anxiety. The Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition, now includes abnormal sensory symptoms as part of the diagnostic criteria for ASD under the category of restricted and repetitive patterns of behavior. In children with ASD, these symptoms can include hypersensitivity or hyposensitivity to sensory input or, alternatively, unusual interest in and seeking out of sensory input.

