## Justice Minister Mmamoloko Kubayi said regulations providing for the payment of the once-off individual reparations grant of R30,000 to victims were published in 2003 and identified just more than 1,600 people as victims at the time.

Minister of Justice Mmamoloko Kubayi said her department has paid out almost R500 million in Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC)-related reparations to date.

Kubayi said regulations providing for the payment of the once-off individual reparations grant of R30,000 to victims were published in 2003 and identified just more than 1,600 people as victims at the time.

She said as of 20 August, 17,560 of the 21,676 victims applied for the once-off grant and were paid out.

Kubayi was responding to questions in the National Council of Provinces (NCOP) about the progress her department has made to date in implementing the TRC reparations and interventions she pronounced during the 2025/26 budget vote.

“This amounts to R498 million overall that has been paid, and also what we have done was to publish the names of the 4,216 people that did not apply, and we did this this year in the newspapers.”

