2023 marked eight years since the release of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission’s 94 Calls to Action and the fifth and final year of authors Eva Jewell and Ian Mosby tracking Canada’s progress on completing those Calls. In this edition of their annual Calls to Action Accountability analysis, Jewell and Mosby reflected on the past five years of reconciliatory movements in Canada. What barriers to reconciliation have been witnessed? What has compelled Canada to act? Who has pushed progress on these Calls to Action forward? As Yellowhead presses on in different areas and ways to push for transformative change, we are grateful for all of the support for this work, and how these reports have been taken up in communities.

