Companies selling products on the European market need to show that their supply chains are deforest ation-free. Fairtrade Standards align with the EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR). And building on a foundation of fair livelihoods and ethical data princi ples, Fairtrade offers companies and producers the support and security to meet EUDR requirements and go beyond compliance to meaningful forest protection. 1. Validated geolocation data: Fairtrade provides hands-on support and digital tools to producer organ isations to collect, conduct quality checks and share geolocation data in the format required by the EUDR TRACES platform. Fairtrade’s Plot Insights tool allows producer organisations to receive near real-time risk analysis where follow up is needed and receive risk analysis reports. 2. Deforestation monitoring data: Fairtrade’s partner, Satelligence, creates a high-quality deforestation risk analysis for each Fairtrade producer organisation. Satelligence uses best-in-class custom satellite imag ing, visualisation, and risk identification technologies, which reduces false positives and generates alerts for plots on or near deforested land or protected areas. 3. Insights for risk assessments: Companies have access to the Fairtrade Risk Map to support their risk assessments. The risk map provides the latest information about deforestation-related risks for the commodities and origins that Fairtrade certifies, with insights validated by producers themselves. Custom ised risk reports on companies’ supply chains can be developed as an additional service.

