The EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR) ensures that relevant commodities entering the EU are deforestation-free and legally sourced. Fairtrade extended both its Cocoa and Coffee Standards by adding EUDR-specific requirements, e.g. geolocation collection. The aim is sharing the burden of meeting the regulation more fairly among all stakeholders in the supply chain. Before placing a product on the EU market or exporting it, operators must submit a Due Diligence Statement (DDS) containing all required geolocation data. If geolocation data is incomplete or absent, the product cannot be placed on the EU market (Article9 EUDR).
