FAIRTRACE by

Reporting & Verifi cation Guidelines

What is Fairtrace?

Fairtrace is FLOCERT’s online collaboration and assurance platform for all certifi ed companies. It is
based on the principle of “virtual handshakes” between supply chain partners: one party reports a
transaction and the other verifi es it – the result is a mutual agreement on correct information.

“Reporting” means entering
your Fairtrade transactions
in the platform.

“Verifi cation” means checking
transactions reported to you
by your business partners
and correcting any errors.

So, as a Fairtrade trader:

You have to report quarterly:

•  all your Fairtrade sales transactions
•   all your Fairtrade direct purchases from

producers

You also have to verify the transactions
reported or corrected by all your Fairtrade
business partners (suppliers, customers).

•   In order to report or verify a transaction, you need to connect with your business partners.

Do so by inviting them to connect with you or by accepting their invite.

•   Only report or verify completed transactions, where the product was delivered and the

Fairtrade Price (and Premium, if relevant) were already paid.

•   For your product reporting, use the product codes available on the platform. If you do not fi nd

your product, please contact us at reporting@fl ocert.net so we can add it.

•   If you are responsible for paying or conveying the Fairtrade Price and/or Premium (i.e you are

a Payer or Conveyer in the Fairtrade Standards) you need to include information about
the Price and Premium paid when you do your reporting.

•   If you are reporting fi nal Fairtrade product sales in the platform Connect, you do not have to

report these sales into Fairtrace as well.

•   If you have not had any Fairtrade transactions in the period you are reporting for or you are not

the reporting party, choose “Nothing to report” in your report declarations.

