relation. Regardless of whether the concept of sufficiency is invoked, the subset 
relation is the key device for pinpointing the different combinations of conditions linked 
in some way to an outcome (e.g., the combinations of conditions linked to democratic 
survival or breakdown in interwar Europe). 
With crisp sets it is a simple matter to determine whether the cases sharing a 
