simply examines cases sharing each combination of conditions and assesses whether or 
not they agree in displaying the outcome. In crisp-set analyses, researchers use truth 
tables to sort cases according to the causal conditions they share, and the investigator 
assesses whether or not the cases in each row of the truth table agree on the outcome. 
