2.2 Causal Models and Directed Acyclic Graphs

In principle, highly complex causal relations can be expressed in potential outcomes notation.
However, for structures involving multiple variables, it can be useful to generate a visual
representation of causal relations. In this section, we show how causal models and directed
acyclic graphs (DAGs) can represent substantive beliefs about how the world works. The
