The MRT subway accepts single journey tickets, contactless bank cards (Visa, Mastercard), and the MRT Plus stored value card. The MRT Plus card costs 180 THB to issue, which includes 100 THB of stored value, and expires five years from the last use. Fares on the Blue and Purple lines range 17 to 70 THB per the published rate by operator BEM, though this figure is revised annually by the regulatory body. Fares on the Yellow and Pink monorail lines run 15 to 45 THB per the annual rate from operator EBM. Contactless bank cards work at the turnstile without purchasing any stored value card.
