TL;DR: Wat Phra That Doi Suthep is Chiang Mai's most sacred temple, a gold-plated chedi on Doi Suthep mountain about 15km from the Old City, founded in 1383 after a legendary white elephant chose the site. Most visitors get there by shared red songthaew from Chang Phueak Gate or Chiang Mai University (roughly ฿40-100 per person depending on the route and how full the truck is), then either climb the 306-step Naga staircase or ride the funicular tram for a small extra fee. Entry runs around ฿30-50 for foreigners depending on the source, and the dress code requires covered shoulders and knees. Go at or before sunrise to beat both the crowds and the haze.
