Plan to spend at least a couple of hours exploring the temple and surrounding area and, if you have more time, there’s the option to hike various trails and swim in waterfalls in the national park that houses the temple. Entrance to the temple costs 50 THB per person. Remember that shoulders and knees need to be covered to enter the temple, so wear a T-shirt and pack a sarong to wrap around your waist. If you forget, wraps are available if needed. You’ll also need to remove your shoes upon entering the temple.
