### Bus A1/A2 + BTS + Boat – Budget Hero

Walk outside Terminal 1 to the main road. Bus stop’s across the street, signed ‘A1 Mo Chit / A2 Victory Monument’. A1 or A2 both work. Board, pay ฿30 cash to the conductor. Ride 30 min to Mo Chit BTS station. Get off, walk into the station, buy a BTS ticket to Saphan Taksin (฿40-50 depending on distance). Skytrain takes 20 min. Exit at Saphan Taksin, walk down to Sathorn Pier. Buy a Chao Phraya Express boat ticket (฿15-40) to your hotel’s nearest pier.

Total cost ฿85-120. Total time 90 min if connections align. Luggage? Manageable if you have one suitcase. Two big bags or traveling with a partner who has bags too? Stairs at BTS stations will hurt. Do this if you’re fit and enjoy the journey. Boat ride’s pretty, you see the Grand Palace and Wat Arun from the water.
