[5] Visa Exemption and Bilateral Agreement | ThaiEmbassy.com (2024-06-18T14:09:42.000Z)
URL: https://www.thaiembassy.com/thailand-visa/thai-visa-exemption-and-bilateral-agreement
Thailand is replacing its 60-day visa exemption with a 30-day exemption and cutting its Visa on Arrival list, effective September 15, 2026.

- Visa Exemption: Cut from 60 to 30 days. Eligible countries cut from 93 to 60. Mauritius and Seychelles keep a separate 15-day exemption.
- Visa on Arrival: Cut from 31 eligible countries to just 3, Azerbaijan, Belarus, and Serbia, still for a 15-day stay.
- Land Border Cap: Visa-exempt travelers entering via land border are limited to 2 entries per calendar year. Malaysia, Brunei, Indonesia, and Singapore are exempt.
- Bilateral Agreements: Countries with existing bilateral agreements with Thailand are unaffected and keep their current 14, 30, or 90-day stay periods.
- Grandfathering: Enter Thailand on or before September 14, 2026, and you keep the 60-day stamp under the current rules.
