[4] Bangkok to Chiang Mai (2026): Sleeper Train, Flight or Bus (2026-07-20T08:00:34.000Z)
URL: https://www.visitthailandtoday.com/guides/bangkok-to-chiang-mai
Bangkok to Chiang Mai is 693 km by road and 751 km by rail. Fly it in 70–80 minutes from about $20 (฿700–1,500) booked a few weeks out, take the overnight sleeper train in 12–14 hours (฿771–1,041, about $23–32, for a second-class berth), or ride an overnight bus in 9–11 hours for ฿650–1,050 ($20–32). The flight is fastest and, with carry-on only, often cheapest. The No. 9 sleeper is the one I'd book if you have a night to spare, because it replaces a hotel night, and it's Thailand's classic rail journey. Below, all three compared with official 2026 fares, every train on the line and which one to pick, what a berth is actually like, the 90-day booking rule that changed in April 2026, where to break the journey, and how to come back.
...
### The sleeper train takes 12–14 hours, ฿771–1,041 ($23–32) for a 2nd-class berth

