[2] Rodecaster Pro 2 (and probably other sound devices): Solution for bad sound after windows update - Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) - mAirList Community Forum (2026-08-23T13:37:56.000Z)
URL: https://community.mairlist.com/t/rodecaster-pro-2-and-probably-other-sound-devices-solution-for-bad-sound-after-windows-update/19453
recently, several users in our forum, in Facebook groups, and some of my own clients have reported bad audio quality with their RØDECaster Pro II after the latest Windows 11 update — without having changed anything themselves beforehand.

After some research, it turned out that Windows had changed the sound device settings by activating “Windows Audio Processing Objects” (APOs) — specifically the enhancement called “Clarity” — because the RØDECaster Pro II is recognized by Windows as a microphone line-in. This affected the entire USB signal chain from the RØDECaster Pro II to the mAirList encoder.

To fix this, please open every input of the RØDECaster Pro II in Windows’ sound settings and disable the “Clarity” enhancement feature (or whatever it’s called in your language).

Step-by-Step:

1. Right-click the speaker icon in the Windows 11 taskbar and select “Sound settings” (or go to Settings → System → Sound).
2. Under “Input”, click on the RØDECaster Pro II input device you want to check.
3. Scroll down to “Input enhancements” (sometimes labeled “Audio enhancements”).
4. If “Clarity” (or a similar enhancement) is enabled, turn it off — or select “Device Default Effects Off” / “Disable all sound effects” if available.
5. Go back to the sound settings overview and repeat steps 2–4 for every remaining input of the RØDECaster Pro II.
6. Also check the “Output” devices the same way, since enhancements can sometimes affect outputs too.

Maybe you need to restart the affected application (e.g., mAirList) to make sure the changes take effect.

PS: This “feature” also affected the two inputs on my own local sound card, so it may impact more devices than you’d expect — it’s worth checking any USB audio interface, not just the RØDECaster.
