The P8 has nine sound pads (each with four virtual banks) compared with the L‑8’s six, and this time they’re treated to their own, dedicated stereo mixer channel. One limitation of the L‑8 is that its sound pads share a stereo channel with line, phone and USB‑C inputs. Instead, on the P8, mic channel 6 doubles up as the USB channel. The P8 is compatible with Mac, Windows, iOS or Android devices, and the USB‑C port allows you to include phone calls or an audio feed to/from VOIP or video‑conference apps (such as Zoom — no relation!) in your podcasts; to use the P8 as a 2‑in/2‑out audio interface; or for file transfer. An adjacent TRRS mini‑jack socket provides a two‑way connection for a smartphone or si…

