If you are experiencing issues with the RØDECaster Pro II or RØDECaster Duo Virtual Devices, follow the steps below to ensure the firmware, driver and Windows audio settings are configured correctly.
...
1. Confirm your RØDECaster is running the latest firmware.
2. Confirm you have installed the latest Virtual Device driver.

 Download: The latest Virtual Device driver is available from the RØDECaster Virtual Devices User Guide .

### 2. Verify the Multitrack Settings
...
Ensure the following options are enabled:

- Expanded USB 1 Input
- Pre/Post Fader USB 1 Output

### 3. Confirm the Virtual Device Is Connected

Open the Virtual Device application from your Windows taskbar or system tray and confirm it is communicating with your RØDECaster.

Also ensure the Bypass option is disabled.

 Please note: If Bypass is enabled, the Virtual Device channels will not communicate with the RØDECaster.
...
### 5. Enable Disabled Audio Devices in Windows

Windows may automatically disable unused playback and recording devices.

1. Open Windows Sound Settings.
2. Select More Sound Settings (Windows 11).
3. Right click within the device list and enable Show Disabled Devices.
4. Enable any disabled RØDECaster playback and recording devices.

 Tip: Check both the Playback and Recording tabs, as Windows may disable devices in either category.

