Implementing DLP policies for unmanaged apps in the browser follows these phases:

1. Create a DLP policy targeting unmanaged apps in the browser (the procedure in this article) in the Microsoft Purview Data Loss Prevention portal.
2. The creation of the DLP policy triggers the Microsoft Edge management service to automatically create the Microsoft Edge configuration policies required to activate DLP policies in Edge for Business. The configuration policies use Microsoft Intune policies to fully activate your Microsoft Purview policies in Microsoft Edge.
3. (optional) Create a collection policy that targets unmanaged apps in the browser to identify other sensitive data sharing across your organization.
