To help you get started with Microsoft Purview data loss prevention (DLP) for the Microsoft 365 Copilot location, Microsoft created a default DLP policy called **Default DLP policy - Protect sensitive M365 Copilot interactions**. The policy is referenced in the **Safeguard sensitive data in Copilot interactions** banner. 
 
Note 
 
See these message center announcements MC1182689 and MC1181998. 
 
Important 
 
The default policy detects sensitive information types (SIT) in user prompts. The **Default DLP policy - Protect sensitive M365 Copilot interactions** is initially configured to **Run the policy in simulation mode** > **Show policy tips while in simulation mode**. This means that the event will only be logged. If you want to block processing of the prompt, you must change the state of the policy to enforce mode. 
 
