### Implement Session Controls via Defender for Cloud Apps

Use Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps to monitor and block real-time file uploads to unsanctioned generative AI applications.

If you want to control sessions and uploads based on conditional access rather than endpoint DLP, Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps provides robust session controls to block uploads to specified cloud services.

Access Cloud Apps policies

Open the Microsoft Defender portal and navigate to 'Cloud Apps' > 'Policies' > 'Policy management'.

Create a session policy

Click 'Create policy' and select 'Session policy'. Choose 'Control file upload (with inspection)' from the policy template dropdown.

Define the AI app filter

Under the 'Activity source' section, add a filter for the specific generative AI applications (e.g., ChatGPT) or filter by app tags if you have categorized AI apps as 'Unsanctioned'.

Set the action to Block

Under the 'Actions' section, select 'Block'. You can also customize the block message that the user will see when attempting to upload a file.
...
Can I block specific users from uploading files rather than the entire organization?

Yes. When configuring Microsoft Purview DLP or Defender for Cloud Apps policies, you can scope the policy to target specific users, Active Directory groups, or specific endpoints instead of applying it tenant-wide.
