﻿# DID Key Recovery Specification (DID-RECOVERY) 
 
The DID Key Recovery specification defines a standardized, interoperable mechanism for recovering control of Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) when private keys are lost or compromised. It introduces three complementary recovery types — Social ZKP Recovery using threshold cryptography with zero-knowledge proofs, Deterministic Seedling Inheritance using hierarchical deterministic keys with VDF-based time-locks, and MPC-Mediated Recovery using multi-party computation with threshold signatures and proactive share refreshment — each addressing different trust models and user personas. This specification is a **CG-DRAFT** being developed by the W3C Credentials Community Group. Contributions and feedback are welcome via the GitHub repository.

