Version 1.4 of the Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) released

The latest version (1.4) of the Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) has been published on Github for public feedback.
...
## Version 1.4 of the Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) released
...
The latest version (1.4) of the Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) has been published on Github for public feedback.

The ARF outlines how wallets distributed by Member States will function and contains a high level overview of the standards and practices that are needed to build the wallet.

The Reference Implementation (open-source code for the wallet), is being built based on the specifications in the ARF.

### What has been updated?

Changes in version 1.4 include:

- Authentic Sources now must provide an interface to Qualified Trusted Service Providers during data verification
- The value of presented attributes now do not have to be included when creating seals or signatures for service providers.

Members of the public are very welcome to contribute by giving their feedback on the ARF on our Github.

