The EUDI Wallet Architecture and Reference Framework (ARF) v3.0.0 aligns the 
framework with the latest amending Implementing Regulations and introduces the 
Functional Conformance Assessment Framework. 
 
## Highlights 
 
- **Alignment with the amending Commission Implementing Regulations** for the 
 core EUDI Wallet framework: PID and EAA (amending CIR 2024/2977), integrity and 
 core functionalities (CIR 2024/2979), ecosystem notifications (CIR 2024/2980), 
 protocols and interfaces (CIR 2024/2982), and the registration of 
 Wallet-Relying Parties (CIR 2025/848). 
- **Relying Party Services** — a new concept from the Topic X revision round 
 (Relying Party registration); see Section 3.11.2 and Topic 44. 
- **Wallet-to-wallet interactions** — changes from the Topic J revision round. 
- **Trust-anchor retrieval** — new requirements for Wallets, Relying Parties, and 
 issuers to support both Trusted Lists (ETSI TS 119 612) and Lists of Trusted 
 Entities / LoTEs (ETSI TS 119 602). 
- **Functional Conformance Assessment Framework (FCAF)** — new Section 7.5 
 introducing a shared, reusable set of test cases for the functional 
 requirements that Wallet Solutions must support, published and maintained at 
 https://conformance.eudi.dev. 
 
## Also in this release 
 
- Many issues raised via Confluence and GitHub have been resolved, together with 
 a number of editorial corrections. 
- The main document is now published as one page per chapter on the website for 
 easier navigation; the combined PDF is unchanged. 
 
## Legal basis — published amending acts 
 
Several of the Implementing Regulations underlying this release have been amended 
by the now-published Commission Implementing Regulations. The title of each 
amending act identifies the Implementing Regulation it ame…
