By notification G.S.R. 846(E) dated 13th November 2025, the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology, acting for the Central Government under sub-sections (1) and (2) of section 40 of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (22 of 2023), makes the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025, after considering public objections to the draft rules published on 3rd January 2025 (G.S.R. 02(E)). Rules 1, 2 and 17 to 21 take effect on the date of publication, rule 4 one year later, and the remaining rules eighteen months later. The rules prescribe the notice a Data Fiduciary must give a Data Principal before processing her personal data; conditions (First Schedule, Part A) and obligations (Part B) for registering and operating Consent Managers, including a minimum seven-year retention of consent records and a fiduciary duty toward Data Principals; standards (Second Schedule) for processing by the State and its instrumentalities to provide subsidies, benefits, services, certificates, licences or permits, and for research, archiving or statistical purposes; minimum security safeguards such as encryption, access control and at least one year's retention of processing logs; breach-intimation duties to affected Data Principals and, within seventy-two hours, to the Data Protection Board of India; timelines and notice requirements for erasing personal data once its specified purpose is served; verifiable-consent procedures for processing a child's personal data and for a person with disability with a lawful guardian, referencing the Information Technology Act, 2000 (21 of 2000), the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (49 of 2016), and the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities…

