Regulation (EU) 2024/1183 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 April 2024 amending Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 as regards establishing the European Digital Identity Framework, commonly referred to as eIDAS 2 or the European Digital Identity Regulation, is a regulation of the European Union that establishes a comprehensive legal framework for a European Digital Identity ecosystem, with the EU Digital Identity Wallet(EUDI Wallet) at its centre. The regulation amends its predecessor, Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 (known as eIDAS), which had governed electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market since 2014.
...
The original eIDAS Regulation (Regulation (EU) No 910/2014) entered into force on 17 September 2014 and applied from 1 July 2016, establishing the first EU-wide legal framework for electronic identification and trust services including electronic signatures, seals, time stamps, and website authentication certificates. The framework allowed notified national electronic identification schemes to be used to access public services online across borders within the EU.
...
The central innovation of the regulation is the European Digital Identity Wallet (EUDI Wallet), a secure mobile application allowing EU citizens, residents and businesses to store, manage and share digital credentials such as identity documents, professional certificates and other personal attributes. The regulation affirms that everyone in the EU has the right to a digital identity under their sole control, enabling participation in the digital economy and exercise of rights in the digital environment.
