Featured is a chess miniature between Emanuel Lasker and Vasja Pirc from 1935. In response to Pirc’s Sicilian Scheveningen, Lasker launches his f-pawn with an eye on the f5-break. Pirc ignores this idea and looks to quickly maneuver his knight to the invasive c4-square. The issue with Pirc’s knight transfer is that it neglects development when the position is about to be cracked open. Lasker’s forceful sequence of follow-up moves decides the game after only 20 moves. #EmanuelLasker
