According to a National Assembly research institute, the rate of use of parental leave has significantly increased due to the effects of government policies, including the 3+3 parental leave system. However, it is pointed out that workers in small and medium-sized businesses or less are still alienated from system benefits, so reinforcement measures are needed.

"The number of parents who used parental leave for every 100 births increased 3.3 (12.4%) for women and 2.0 (66.7%) for men in 2022 compared to the previous year," the National Assembly Future Institute said in a statement released on the 2nd. "It is believed to be due to the newly implemented '3+3 parental parental leave system'."

According to Statistics Korea's parental leave statistics cited by the researcher, the number of parents on parental leave per 100 births was 26.7 women and 3.0 men in 2021, but increased to 30.0 and 5.0 respectively in 2022.

The researcher evaluated this significant change as the effect of the '3+3 parental leave system'. This system was a system in which couples pay the upper limit of parental leave benefits when they use parental leave within 12 months of the age of their children together. The payment was increased from 80% to 100% of ordinary wages, and the upper limit was raised from 1.5 million won to 2 million won in the first month, 2.5 million won in the second month and 3 million won in the third month.

The system began with the Moon Jae-in administration, and the Yoon Seok-yeol administration expanded it and has been implementing the "6+6 Parental Leave System" since this year. The application target has also been increased to within 18 months of the age of children, and if both parents use parental leave, the upper limit of parental leave benefits will be increased fr…

