### Recent Reforms (2018-2019)

Mobility: Saudi Arabia made going places easier for women by removing restrictions on obtaining a passport and traveling abroad. New legal amendments also equalized a woman’s right to choose where to live and leave the marital home.

Workplace: Saudi Arabia enacted legislation and criminal penalties for sexual harassment in employment. It also 
prohibited gender discrimination in employment. 
Marriage: Saudi Arabia began allowing women to be head of household and removed the legal obligation for a 
married woman to obey her husband. 
Parenthood: Saudi Arabia prohibited the dismissal of pregnant workers. 
Entrepreneurship: Saudi Arabia made access to credit easier for women by prohibiting gender-based 
discrimination in access to financial services. 
Pension: Saudi Arabia equalized the age (60 years) at which men and women can retire with full pension 
benefits. It also mandated a retirement age of 60 years for both women and men.
